ector’s ingest format, for an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to send."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"CollectorEncoding"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChoosingDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","title":"Choosing Destinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues":{"url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","abstract":[{"text":"The sequence type of every report and delivery stream the library hands out, and of an app’s own, read by one task at a time.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"AsyncQueues"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://JSONValues/documentation/JSONValues":{"url":"\/documentation\/jsonvalues","identifier":"doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues","abstract":[{"text":"A JSON value that renders to the same bytes on every platform and Swift release.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"JSONValues"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","title":"TrackingPlans","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON":{"url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","title":"PropertyJSON","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The vendor-neutral pieces a JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is built from: properties, context, timestamps, identity and batch splitting.","type":"text"}]},"doc://TelemetryDeckEncoding/documentation/TelemetryDeckEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to TelemetryDeck as signals, through its Ingest API v3."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"},"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding","title":"AptabaseEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to Aptaba